$post_body = <<<'HTML'
<p>Roller shades are typically less expensive than custom wood or faux wood blinds per window. Basic panel shades can also come in under blind pricing. Plantation shutters and custom draperies generally cost more than blinds per window.</p>
<p>Understanding where blinds sit in the wider price landscape helps you make sense of the choices available before a consultation. Here's how the main window treatment categories compare on upfront price.</p>
%IMAGE1%
<h2 id="how-window-treatment-categories-compare-on-price">How Window Treatment Categories Compare on Price?</h2>
<p>The pricing comparison below uses custom-fit products because that's the meaningful comparison. Off-the-shelf products from a hardware store sit in their own category and aren't comparable to professionally measured and installed window treatments.</p>
<p>From least to most expensive per window, the general order is: roller shades in standard fabric, horizontal blinds (aluminum then faux wood then real wood), roman shades and honeycomb shades, plantation shutters, and custom draperies with hardware. That order shifts based on specific materials, window size, and finish choices, but it holds as a general pattern.</p>
<h2 id="roller-shades-usually-less-expensive-than-custom-blinds">Roller Shades: Usually Less Expensive Than Custom Blinds</h2>
<p>Custom roller shades in standard fabrics typically cost less per window than custom faux wood or real wood blinds of the same size. The mechanism is simpler (one tube, one fabric, no slats), the production process is more straightforward, and the range of standard fabrics is wide enough that you don't need premium options to get a good result.</p>
<p>The pricing advantage narrows when you add motorization, premium natural fabrics, or blackout liners to roller shades. At that point, the price overlap with quality blinds becomes significant.</p>
<p>Our <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/shades/roller-shades/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">roller shades</a> start at a lower price point than our faux wood blind range for most standard window sizes.</p>
<h2 id="other-shades-that-often-cost-less-than-blinds">Other Shades That Often Cost Less Than Blinds</h2>
<p>Sheer shades in basic fabric weights can come in at or below the price of faux wood blinds. They're a single-layer product with a simple mechanism and don't require the same material volume as a slatted blind.</p>
<p>Honeycomb cellular shades are in a similar range as quality horizontal blinds. You're choosing between them based on function and look, not because one is clearly cheaper.</p>
<p>Our full <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/shades/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">shades</a> range covers all shade product families with pricing discussed during each free in-home consultation.</p>
<h2 id="what-costs-more-than-blinds">What Costs More Than Blinds?</h2>
<p>Plantation shutters are the most expensive window treatment category per window. They're permanently installed, made from solid or composite wood, and require more installation time. The upfront cost is higher than any blind or shade product. On a per-year basis over their 20-plus-year lifespan, the cost comparison changes, but the upfront price is real.</p>
<p>Custom draperies with professional installation and curtain hardware also tend to cost more than a basic blind or shade package for the same window, particularly when lining and specialty pleat styles are involved.</p>
<p>Our <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/window-shutters/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">window shutters</a> are the premium option and are priced accordingly. During your consultation, we'll confirm whether they're in range for your project.</p>
<h2 id="what-falls-in-the-same-range-as-blinds">What Falls in the Same Range as Blinds?</h2>
<p>Roman shades and quality honeycomb shades cost roughly the same as quality horizontal blinds per window. These aren't cheaper alternatives to blinds in most configurations. The decision between them is about function and appearance, not price.</p>
<p>Vertical blinds for wide windows and sliding doors typically fall in a similar range as horizontal blinds for the same opening size.</p>
<h2 id="a-note-on-total-value-not-just-upfront-price">A Note on Total Value, Not Just Upfront Price</h2>
<p>Upfront price is one dimension of what window treatments actually cost. A product that costs 30% less but needs replacing in four years instead of eight costs more over time, and the replacement requires a new consultation, a new order, and new installation.</p>
<p>For a guide to which specific blind products deliver the best value within the blinds category over the long term, our most cost-effective blinds guide covers that analysis in detail.</p>
<p>Our <a href="%BASE%/guidelines/precision-measurement/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">precision measurement guide</a> explains why a correctly fitted product delivers more value than a cheaper product that doesn't fit your window.</p>
%IMAGE2%
<h2 id="getting-the-right-price-for-your-window-treatment-in-aurora-">Getting the Right Price for Your Window Treatment in Aurora, IL</h2>
<p>Creative Blinds and Drapes installs window treatments across a range of price points in Aurora, IL and surrounding communities. Our free in-home consultation covers what's available at your budget across all product categories.</p>
<p>See our service coverage on the <a href="%BASE%/service-areas/aurora-il/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">service areas page</a> or contact us to book your free consultation.</p>
